Implemented the missing “screen-owned” legacy behaviors for `claims-mgmt-v1/home` by wiring up the hidden-at-rest panels (MCB + AAG overlays) that the Provider kit can’t infer from markup alone.

**Changes**
- Added legacy function bindings + panel open/close logic in `src/screens/home/legacy.ts`.
  - Defines window functions used by `href="javascript:..."` links: `toggleVisibility`, `toggleVisibilityStyle`, `getAudit/getMail/getNotes/getPrintPreview/getReports/getReturnToProvider`, `getFavorites/getContactUs/getBroadcastMsg`, `popupCenteredWindow`.
  - Adds click-capture handlers to close MCB panels (`#auditClose`, `#mailClose`, etc.) and AAG panels (`#ExternalLinksClose`, `#FavoritesClose`, etc.).
  - Forces Provider-flavor message instructions when opening Messages.
- Hooked the bindings into the page in `src/screens/home/Page.tsx:3` and `src/screens/home/Page.tsx:12`.

**TypeScript check**
- `npx tsc --noEmit` reports errors in `src/screens/search-claims/**` only; no remaining TS errors from `src/screens/home/**`.

**Verify**
- Tried running the required verify command, but `node scripts/verify.mjs` fails with `ERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED` to `http://localhost:5180/#/`, so no `packs/claims-mgmt-v1/screens/home/verify/report.json` was produced.

Skipped: implementing expand/collapse behavior for the accessory panels (only open/close), and I did not start/restart the dev server to satisfy the “never start/stop it” rule—risk is the verify step couldn’t be completed in this environment.
